# Performance Testing

## 1. Testing Objective

The objective of testing is to verify that the configured ACLs correctly enforce the required access permissions for the `u_institution_details` table.

## 2. READ Testing

The READ ACL is tested using users with different roles and access conditions.

The test verifies whether users can view the records they are permitted to access.

## 3. CREATE Testing

The CREATE ACL is tested to verify whether authorized users can create new institution records and unauthorized users are prevented from doing so.

## 4. WRITE Testing

The WRITE ACL is tested by attempting to modify existing records with users having different permissions.

The test verifies that only permitted users can modify records.

## 5. DELETE Testing

The DELETE ACL is tested to verify whether users with the required permissions can delete records.

Unauthorized users should not be able to delete restricted records.

## 6. Unauthorized Access Testing

Users without the required permissions are tested against the configured ACLs.

The system should deny operations when the applicable ACL requirements are not satisfied.

## 7. Administrator Testing

Administrator access is tested to verify that administrators can perform the required management and configuration activities.

## 8. Testing Result

The ACLs are evaluated for each operation and the access decision is based on the configured roles and conditions.

The testing confirms that the project provides controlled access to the institution records.

## 9. Conclusion

Performance and functional testing help verify that the Script-Controlled ACL solution operates consistently and enforces the intended access-control rules.

